Agenda SR70
===========

The application uses System V message queues/shared memory and SDL2, so it
must be built and run on Linux.

Install the required packages on Debian/Ubuntu:

    sudo apt install build-essential libsdl2-dev libsdl2-ttf-dev fonts-dejavu-core

Build from this directory:

    gcc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic launcher.c gestionnaire.c member.c ui.c -lSDL2_ttf -lSDL2 -o agenda

Run:

    ./agenda

The window contains the shared room schedule, team/member pages, meeting
requests, meeting deletion, and the manager-maintained event history. Closing
the window stops the manager and member child processes.
